  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "SOLVED (PR #34063). Assembled the classical closed form for the binary bracelet numbers b(n)=A000029(n) via the dihedral Burnside sum: braceletClosed n = (rotTerm n + reflTerm n)/(2n), with rotTerm n = Σ_{i:ZMod n} 2^gcd(n,i.val) and reflTerm n = n·2^((n+1)/2) (odd n) / (n/2)·2^(n/2+1)+(n/2)·2^(n/2) (even n). Proved rotTerm_eq (rotation term = true rotation fixed-point total, all n), validated the full formula against the genuine dihedral orbit count for n=3..6 (b(3)=4,b(4)=6 fresh; b(5)=8,b(6)=13 imported), and predicted b(7)=18,b(8)=30,b(9)=46,b(10)=78 by arithmetic. Axiom-free (no native_decide). New file Proofs/BurnsideCountingOQ04OQ01OQ02.lean, 189 lines, builds clean on Mathlib 4.26.0.",
    "builtItems": [
      "braceletClosed n = (rotTerm n + reflTerm n)/(2n): explicit closed form for b(n)",
      "rotTerm_eq: rotTerm n = Σ_i |Fix(r i)| for all n (computation-free, via card_rotFixed)",
      "braceletClosed_eq_orbitCount_{three,four,five,six}: formula = true orbit count for n=3,4,5,6",
      "fixed_sum_three/bracelet_three (b(3)=4) and fixed_sum_four/bracelet_four (b(4)=6): fresh Burnside counts",
      "bracelet_seven..ten: b(7)=18,b(8)=30,b(9)=46,b(10)=78 predicted by the closed form"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Burnside over D_n splits the bracelet count into a rotation total (= n·necklaces = Σ 2^gcd(n,i)) and a reflection total with an odd/even dichotomy",
      "The rotation half anchors to the true fixed-point counts for ALL n via the sibling's card_rotFixed=2^gcd(n,i.val); only the reflection half remains to be made generic",
      "Validating the closed form against the machine-checked orbit quotient (n<=6, both parities) is stronger than an OEIS lookup, and the formula then reaches lengths where decide on the quotient is infeasible"
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Prove the reflection fixed-point count generically: |Fix(sr i)| = 2^(orbits of x↦-i-x) = 2^((n+1)/2) (odd n) / 2^(n/2+1) or 2^(n/2) (even n, by parity of i), via Burnside on the order-2 subgroup <sr i> plus a quotient bijection RefFixed n i ≃ (ZMod n/<sr i> → Fin 2)",
      "Combine with rotTerm_eq to prove braceletClosed n = A000029(n) as a theorem for ALL n",
      "Generalise to k colours: rotTerm becomes Σ k^gcd(n,i), reflTerm k^((n+1)/2)/k^(n/2+1)/k^(n/2)"
    ]
  },
